  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">for the SDGs Today program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable Development Goals Today (SDGs Today) is a data and geospatial program of the Sustainable Development Solutions Network (SDSN) that was launched at the UN High-Level Political Forum in 2020 in partnership with Esri (a leading organization devising geo-information solutions), and the National Geographic Society. It works to advance the production and use of timely geospatial data for the SDGs. SDGs Today provides a snapshot of the state of sustainable development around the world, and fosters data partnerships to co-develop interactive, accessible, and timely data products. The team co-designs real-world applications and stories to humanize quantitative data and communicates the impact of nontraditional data on decision making to various stakeholder groups. This grant will support SDGs Today as it integrates several inclusive data research initiatives of the Thematic Research Network on Data and Statistics (TReNDS), another SDSN program that operated from 2015 to 2024 and was previously supported by the Hewlett Foundation before being wound down. (Strategy: Evidence-Informed Policymaking)</narrative>
  </description>
